<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese tax receipts rise yr/yr Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Portuguese tax receipts rise yr/yr Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese tax receipts rose a nominal 12 percent year-on-year in the first five months of the 1997 to 1.62 trillion escudos, although the rise was nine percent when special factors were taken into account, the Finance Ministry said.</p>
<p>These special factors represented differences in the timings of certain tax payments compared with 1996, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The following table gives a breakdown of tax receipts (in billions of escudos):.</p>
<p>				JAN-MAY 97     JAN-MAY 96    Pct change:</p>
<p>    Direct taxes	    648.2	    614.4	    5.5</p>
<p>    IRS (income tax)	416.0	    432.3  (Not comparable)</p>
<p>    IRC (corporate tax)   232,2	    182,0  (Not comparable)</p>
<p>    Indirect taxes	  941.2	    805.0	   16.9</p>
<p>    VAT			 543.5	    414.4	   31.2</p>
<p>    Stamp duty		 79.1	     75.9	    4.3</p>
<p>    Petrol tax		178.1	    179.5	   -0.7</p>
<p>    Car tax		    71.7	     65.3	    9.8</p>
<p>    Tobacco tax		68.7	     70.0	   -1.8</p>
<p>    Other receipts	   33.4	     29.6	   12.7</p>
<p>    Total		   1,622.8	  1,449.0	   12.0</p>
<p>Percentage of 1997</p>
<p>    budget		     40.3	     39.5</p>
<p>NOTE - The 1996 budget did not come into effect until the second quarter of the year so direct tax levels for the early months of the year are not comparable.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113126</p>
